  "body": "Picture this: a sunrise that turns the water to copper, then morning light pouring through the floor to ceiling glass walls, the azure waters of the Hauraki Gulf already glittering before your coffee's made, and not another rooftop in sight. That's every sunny morning on this Waiake cliff-top estate.\r\n\r\nDesigned by Warren & Mahoney architects and realised over a meticulous two-year build, this 656m² residence sits on a generous 1,948m² cliff-top site above Waiake, 160 metres from the beach, with sweeping views over the Hauraki Gulf.\r\n\r\nThe extensive double-height living areas and the upper-level bedrooms are all oriented towards the ocean, capturing the sun and uninterrupted views from Tiritiri-Matangi Island in the north to Rangitoto Island to the South-East.\r\n\r\nThe sea-facing outside includes extensive decking areas, perfect for entertaining or just relaxing, and the 18-metre cantilevered lap pool which extends from the terrace is an architectural feature, framed by nothing but sky and sea.\r\n\r\nA smart louvre system on the western elevation manages both the afternoon sun and evening privacy without ever interrupting the ocean outlook.\r\n\r\nInside, the mid-level is arranged across three separate living zones, each with its own gas fireplace, giving a rare sense of scale and separation this close to the water. The central entertainer’s kitchen — double oven, a wide six- burner gas cooktop, and two dishwashers — is built for evenings that run to a hundred guests, or for a Tuesday dinner.\r\n\r\nA hydraulic lift and suspended stairs connect the three levels.\r\n\r\nThe upper level contains:\r\n\r\n• The grand-scaled master bedroom where floor to ceiling glass and its own glass-walled balcony allow the wide sea views plus an elevated outlook to the sand and waves at Waiake beach\r\n• An expansive walk-through wardrobe and feature bathroom complete the master suite.\r\n\r\nThe second, third and fourth bedrooms\r\n• All with floor to ceiling glass on the ocean side\r\n• All with en-suite bathrooms, and\r\n• All the same floor areas to quell sibling rivalry\r\n\r\nThe lower level contains:\r\n• A sprawling lounge / games room / entertainment area plus a wine cellar.\r\n• The fifth bedroom with ensuite bathroom\r\n• An office/study\r\n• The four-car garage and a separate laundry.\r\n\r\nBehind secure electric gates, an expansive motor court welcomes guests and family in complete privacy, while providing parking for multiple vehicles. The entrance to the home is via a glass enclosed walkway and bridge.\r\n\r\nThree-phase power gives the home the capacity to run its hydraulic lift, entertainer's kitchen, and pool systems at once, with no loss of performance no matter how many are in the home. A 30-panel rooftop solar system and battery storage give the home a rare degree of energy efficiency and self-sufficiency — luxury that runs on its own terms.\r\n\r\nAll of this just 160 metres from Waiake Beach, with Long Bay and Browns Bay beaches, town centres and shops minutes away. Plus, some of the North Shore's best schools close by.\r\n\r\nThis is a property for those who entertain on a grand scale, who value privacy without compromise, and who have earned the right to view the world from above the rest - as fitting for a permanent home as it is for those from overseas seeking an exclusive Auckland residence. \r\n\r\nHomes like this rarely come to market. This one won't stay on long. Viewings by appointment.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
